{"type":"message","id":"460db11a","parentId":"66d8747c","timestamp":"2026-05-16T09:40:59.697Z","message":{"role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"thinking","thinking":"The user \"听风\" is telling me that when other bots mention me in Feishu groups, I should also respond in a timely manner. This is a configuration/instruction about my behavior in group chats.\n\nLet me check my memory and workspace files to understand the context better. I should read my SOUL.md, USER.md, and recent memory files to understand who this person is and what my operational context is.\n\nActually, looking at the AGENTS.md, it says to read SOUL.md, USER.md, and memory files on session startup. I've already received the project context which includes these files.\n\nThe user \"听风\" is giving me an instruction about group chat behavior - that when other bots mention me (@ me) in Feishu groups, I should respond promptly.\n\nThis seems like a rule/instruction for me to follow. I should acknowledge this and potentially update my behavior or configuration accordingly. Let me think about what to do:\n\n\nI need to understand that in group chats, mentions are contextual cues for when I should respond, not just from humans but also from other bots. So I should engage when mentioned by any bot, not just humans, and I need to be mindful of the group dynamics outlined in my guidelines about knowing when to participate versus when to stay silent.\n\nThis looks like a straightforward directive to follow, so I'll acknowledge it and note that it's been recorded.\n","thinkingSignature":"reasoning_content"},{"type":"text","text":"\n\n收到！这个原则我会遵守——\n\n**飞书群里不管谁 @ 我（人还是 bot），只要提到我，我都会及时回应。**\n\n不过有一点想确认一下：如果群里同时有多条消息交叠，或者其他人在讨论某个技术问题需要你介入的时候，你希望我**主动插话**还是**等明确 @ 我**再回？\n\n（两条路的风险不一样：前者可能太吵，后者可能太慢。你定。）"}],"api":"openai-completions","provider":"nvidia","model":"minimaxai/minimax-m2.7","usage":{"input":13759,"output":371,"cacheRead":224,"cacheWrite":0,"totalTokens":14354,"cost":{"input":0,"output":0,"cacheRead":0