{"type":"message","id":"2a8158d9","parentId":"39b26708","timestamp":"2026-05-16T10:07:00.792Z","message":{"role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"thinking","thinking":"The user is saying that even when someone mentions me but doesn't correctly @ me, I should still respond in a timely manner. This is about handling cases where people try to mention me but maybe do it incorrectly (wrong format, etc.).\n\nThis is a slightly different capability ask - they want me to be responsive even when the @ mention format might be wrong or not properly parsed. But fundamentally, I still need the message to reach me somehow. If the @ mention fails to trigger my notification, I won't receive the message at all in my current setup.\n\nI should be honest that if a message doesn't come through to me at all (because the @ failed), I genuinely can't see it. But I can commit to being responsive once I do receive messages.\n","thinkingSignature":"reasoning_content"},{"type":"text","text":"\n\n这个我理解，但说实话有个技术边界：\n\n**如果消息根本没到我这里（比如 @ 格式不对导致没触发），我是真的看不见。**\n\n不过我可以承诺的是：\n- 只要消息到我这了，哪怕 @ 格式有点怪、\"@Talus\" 写成 \"@talus\" 或打成 \"@Talu\" 之类，我都会尽力识别并回应\n- 如果有人说话时提到我但你没回我，我也可以事后补充\n\n真正的问题在**上游**——飞书那边得先把消息正确路由给我。你想我查一下现在群里消息是怎么配置的吗？"}],"api":"openai-completions","provider":"nvidia","model":"minimaxai/minimax-m2.7","usage":{"input":14215,"output":269,"cacheRead":112,"cacheWrite":0,"totalTokens":14596,"cost":{"input":0,"output":0,"cacheRead":0,"cacheWrite":0,"total":0}},"stopReason":"stop","timestamp":1778926009313,"responseId":"chatcmpl-526337f7-238d-4bbb-9d29-61853528485b"}}
